cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "textblast: text reuse detection with a patched NCBI BLAST engine"
version: 0.9.0
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23729155
repository-code: "https://github.com/Solemne-ERC/textblast"
abstract: >-
  textblast detects text reuse in historical document collections. The method is not new: textblast is a newer and
  faster implementation of the method of Vesanto et al. (2017) and their tool textreuse-blast. It normalizes and
  encodes texts as protein-like sequences, aligns them with NCBI BLAST+ patched for text as in textreuse-blast (a
  uniform match/mismatch matrix and matching gap costs), and maps every hit back to exact character offsets of the
  input. It then joins, defragments, annotates, filters and
  clusters the hits, and exports tables and formats for analysis. It works on any collection of texts in the Latin
  script, given as JSON Lines.
authors:
